  "surprise": "P23-family squared-ReLU MLP (bf16 autograd.Function, parameter-identical) on 153-claude scored 672/632/642 on seeds 0/1/2 vs 676/700/685: exact means 648.67 vs 687.00, -38.3, paired -4/-68/-43. Discard; inside the registered -40..+40 but far below the central +8. The systems half worked: keeping relu^2 in bf16 removed 076-claude's 1.31x step-time penalty (pods logged 682/688/535 steps at 60 s vs 153's 691-726; s2 was a slow pod), pretraining ran 4369/4365/4043 steps (mean 4259 vs 4503, -5.4%, inside the registered 4,250-4,600 band), and RL sampling was unchanged at 225-314 samples/s (the 60 s bench's 114/s was a runaway-sample artefact of an immature model), totals 1712/1569/1820 s. Pretraining quality looked normal: final val 0.0825/0.0831/0.0886 (mean 0.0847, under the 0.089 line), held-out greedy 0.967/0.947/0.9655 (s1 just under the registered 0.95). The loss is in RL: round-1 targets solved 683/210/681 vs 153's 766/747/694, with seed 1's round-1 sample_acc 0.048 (a near-collapse of the T=0.8 sampler at handoff), and RL-solved totals 1145/1092/1130 (mean 1122 vs 1172). Eval shape: ge10 99/98/97, ge11 22/22/23, L* 12 on every seed (153 s0: 109, 26, L* 11), so the frontier was not worse but the bulk at 7-9 was. Reading: relu^2's per-step learning advantage (076) does not survive the Lean/Muon/Peri-LN recipe as a downstream gain; the registered failure mode (a), sharper sparse units giving a less useful T=0.8 sampler at handoff, fits seed 1 and the lower round-1 harvests. With 161-fable2's SwiGLU (-52 vs its incumbent), both MLP-nonlinearity swaps off GELU lost on this recipe.",
